# Pinned `spec` revision the conformance runner validates against.
#
# The runner refuses to run if the spec checkout it is given is not at this
# commit (override with --allow-spec-drift when deliberately testing against
# unreleased vocabulary). Without a pin the suite silently tracks whatever is
# on spec `main`, so a run that passed yesterday can pass today for a
# different reason.
#
# ############ TEMPORARY BRANCH PIN -- MUST BE RE-PINNED BEFORE MERGE ############
# The commit below is the HEAD of the spec BRANCH that carries core v3.6 /
# health v2.7 / clinical v1.15. It is NOT on spec main yet. Once the spec PR
# merges, re-pin this to the spec MERGE COMMIT and its tags
# (vocab/core-v3.6, vocab/health-v2.7, vocab/clinical-v1.15), re-run the suite,
# and confirm the counts in this repo's PR body are unchanged. CI clones
# `commit=` from the public spec repo, so CI on this branch cannot pass until
# that re-pin happens; that is deliberate and is the signal that the merge order
# is spec first, this repo second.
# ###############################################################################
#
# To re-pin: check out the new spec revision, put its full SHA and its
# VOCAB_VERSIONS line below, run `make -C . conformance` (or
# `scripts/run_conformance.py`), and record the resulting counts in the PR.

